  "reviewedFindings": [
    "All 26 actual native WebKit common originals were personally inspected and their original bytes/hash bindings verified. Both completed native reports passed against the identical frozen runtime/data snapshot.",
    "All 32 clubs are supported; completed REG team-game windows, statistical GP, true QB starts and opponent histories use distinct source-backed units. DNP and unavailable values remain null; no five-game padding or relief-appearance starter inference.",
    "Displayed Dallas/Tampa leaders, Godwin five-team-game receiving log, Dak/Jalon QB start metrics, team H2H scores and filtered averages agree with preserved source-derived facts. Hurst disputed targets remain unavailable without discarding agreeing yards.",
    "Live Week 5 research fixture is a dated, attributed ESPN snapshot, with score/clock and current provider-reported availability. Partial live statistics are excluded from completed historical windows.",
    "Repeated future Week 6 INACTIVE objects remain dated team bulletins, without future game-day confirmation or invented QB projection. The regression also advances core week while retaining exact real archived reports.",
    "26 actual meaningful unit tests and all three builder check modes passed. All 94 source archives, 38 existing qualifier outcomes and 235 runtime file bytes were verified unchanged by updater hardening.",
    "Independent specialists verified 712248 numeric/raw-source assertions and 1549 fixture-context assertions with zero failures against this exact book."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Scheduled source refreshes and manual refresh expose retrieval/publication age; this is not an instantaneous provider push feed.",
    "Routes, pressure/blitz splits, complete official inactive coverage, unsupported weather units and unsupported travel details stay unavailable. Provider-reported INACTIVE is not represented as complete official confirmation.",
    "Native browser emulation covers 393/430 phones plus Chromium 768/1440 layouts; a physical iPhone was not tested. Local HTTP browser success does not establish actual hosted HTTPS deployment.",
    "The supplied render is visual authority, not factual authority; its illustrative names, ranks and values were replaced only by verified data. Exact original reference-image bytes were not available for an automated pixel-difference claim."
  ],
